  "chapter": {
    "number": 50,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(51) For the end, a Psalm of David, when Nathan the prophet came to him, when he had gone to Bersabee."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Have mercy upon me, O God, according to your great mercy; and according to the multitude of your compassions blot out my transgression.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Wash me thoroughly from my iniquity, and cleanse me from my sin.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For I am conscious of my iniquity; and my sin is continually before me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Against you only have I sinned, and done evil before you: that you might be justified in your sayings, and might overcome when you are judged.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For, behold, I was conceived in iniquities, and in sins did my mother conceive me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For, behold, you love truth: you have manifested to me the secret and hidden things of your wisdom.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You shall sprinkle me with hyssop, and I shall be purified: you shall wash me, and I shall be made whiter than snow.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You shall cause me to hear gladness and joy: the afflicted bones shall rejoice.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Turn away your face from my sins, and blot out all my iniquities.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit in my inward parts.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Cast me not away from your presence; and remove not your holy Spirit from me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Restore to me the joy of your salvation: establish me with your",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 96
          },
          {
            "text": "directing Spirit.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Then will I teach transgressors your ways; and ungodly men shall turn to you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver me from blood-guiltiness, O God, the God of my salvation: and my tongue shall joyfully declare your righteousness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, you shall open my lips; and my mouth shall declare your praise.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For if you desired sacrifice, I would have given it: you will not take pleasure in whole burnt offerings.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Sacrifice to God is a broken spirit: a broken and humbled heart God will not despise.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Do good, O Lord, to Sion in your good pleasure; and let the walls of Jerusalem be built.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Then shall you be pleased with a sacrifice of righteousness,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 97
          },
          {
            "text": "offering, and whole burnt sacrifices: then shall they offer calves upon your altar.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 96,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. governing.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 50,
          "verse": 12
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 97,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Properly, a heave or wave-offfering.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 50,
          "verse": 19
        }
      }
    ]
  },
